WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.640
All right friends.

00:04.640 --> 00:09.640
So with that, we have covered now the first type of the tables that we have in databases that permanent

00:09.680 --> 00:14.200
tables where you create a table and it's going to live forever until you go and drop it.

00:14.240 --> 00:17.520
Now we're going to talk about another type of tables in databases.

00:17.520 --> 00:19.400
We have the temporary tables.

00:19.480 --> 00:22.040
So let's understand what are temporary tables.

00:22.120 --> 00:26.200
So temporary tables or sometimes you call them as a shortcut temp tables.

00:26.200 --> 00:32.080
They store intermediate results in a temporary storage in the database during a session.

00:32.080 --> 00:37.080
And the database automatically dropped these tables after the session ends.

00:37.200 --> 00:38.960
So let's understand what this means.

00:39.000 --> 00:44.720
Now we have learned in the cities we could use a query in order to retrieve data from one table.

00:44.720 --> 00:49.640
And then it puts the intermediate results in brand new table in the database.

00:49.640 --> 00:52.920
So with that we are creating another table based on a query.

00:52.920 --> 00:55.240
The same thing for that temporary tables.

00:55.240 --> 00:59.200
We have as well a query that goes and retrieve the data from a table.

00:59.200 --> 01:04.760
And as well the database is going to go and create a new brand table in the database that has the structure

01:04.760 --> 01:07.560
and the data from the result of the query.

01:07.560 --> 01:09.560
So it is exactly as the city's.

01:09.560 --> 01:09.640
is.

01:09.680 --> 01:10.880
What is the difference here?

01:11.000 --> 01:13.760
Well, it is about the lifetime of the table.

01:13.800 --> 01:19.720
Now, the database tables that we have created using create, insert or CTAs, those tables can stay

01:19.720 --> 01:24.800
permanent and they can live in the database as long as you don't drop them.

01:24.920 --> 01:31.000
So even if the system is completely offline, the data can stay in the database once it is online again,

01:31.000 --> 01:37.960
but the temporary tables can get deleted and dropped from the database automatically once the session

01:37.960 --> 01:38.480
ends.

01:38.600 --> 01:40.080
So what session means?

01:40.120 --> 01:45.280
Like once you open the client and you connect to the database and you are start doing queries.

01:45.320 --> 01:50.960
We call the time between connecting ourselves to the database and disconnecting from the database.

01:51.000 --> 01:52.280
We call this a session.

01:52.320 --> 01:56.480
So that means once you close the client and you disconnect from the database and maybe shut down your

01:56.480 --> 01:58.360
PC and do something else, what can happen?

01:58.360 --> 02:04.840
The database is going to go and destroy and delete all the temporary tables that you have created during

02:04.840 --> 02:05.480
the session.

02:05.520 --> 02:10.440
So that means the table can live as long as you have a session, and you can access during this time

02:10.440 --> 02:13.480
the table as you are accessing any other permanent table.

02:13.600 --> 02:16.320
So this is what we mean with temporary tables.

02:16.320 --> 02:18.160
Or sometimes you call it as a shortcut.

02:18.200 --> 02:19.160
Temp tables.
